    "id": "9e54d9dea11130be5ffc043258b666e85a717912",
    "message": "Prepare repository for public open-source release\n\nCI: add .github/workflows/ci.yml -- runs on push/PR to main plus manual\ndispatch, installs via the documented `pip install -e \".[dev]\"`, runs the\nfull pytest suite across Python 3.10-3.14 on Linux and at the Python\nfloor/ceiling on Windows, and builds+uploads sdist/wheel artifacts after\ntests pass. Actions are pinned to full commit SHAs resolved from each\naction's actual latest stable GitHub release (checkout v7.0.1, setup-python\nv7.0.0, upload-artifact v7.0.2), not guessed. Workflow permissions are\ncontents: read only; no secrets, cluster access, or AI-provider calls appear\nanywhere in it.\n\nMaintenance: add .github/dependabot.yml for weekly pip and github-actions\nupdate checks.\n\nLicense: added LICENSE (Apache-2.0, the owner's explicit choice) and wired\nit into pyproject.toml (license, license-files, classifiers) -- confirmed\nvia a clean `python -m build` that the built wheel's metadata correctly\nreports License-Expression: Apache-2.0. Added CONTRIBUTING.md and\nSECURITY.md (the latter points to GitHub's private vulnerability reporting\nrather than inventing a contact email).\n\nREADME: rewritten as a proper landing page -- CI/license/Python-version\nbadges, a tightened value proposition and \"what makes it different\"\nparagraph, a Mermaid pipeline diagram, a consolidated \"Key capabilities\"\nlist, and a new \"Example output\" section built from this repository's own\nreal, committed synthetic bundle (never fabricated). Removed a hardcoded,\nstale-prone test count in favor of pointing at the new CI badge/workflow.\n\nFixed a pre-existing credibility defect found while auditing the README for\nthis release: roughly 15 README references pointed at specific files under\ndocs/ that have never been part of this repository's git history (docs/ has\nalways been excluded from commits per this project's own established\npolicy), so every one of those links was dead for a cloned, public copy of\nthis repo. Published the 7 docs/research/*.md files the owner explicitly\nauthorized for public release (scanned for secrets/internal hostnames/\npersonal data first -- none found) and rewrote the remaining references\n(phase-N implementation-note citations, the Project layout entry, and the\nDocumentation section) to only point at what is now actually public,\ninstead of silently committing the rest of docs/ or leaving the dead links\nin place.\n\nSecurity audit (git history + current tree): no credentials, API keys,\nprivate key material, or real reachable hostnames found via pattern search\nacross the full history. One pre-existing, non-blocking item is worth the\nowner's awareness: a widely-reused test fixture constant\n(`_FAKE_DSN = \"postgresql://postgres:postgres@192.168.49.1:5432/devops_genai\"`,\npresent in ~10 test files across the whole history) uses Minikube's own\nwell-known default host IP and trivial default Postgres credentials -- not a\nworking secret or a real host -- but its database-name component echoes the\nname of a separate, unrelated internal platform this project's own CLAUDE.md\nexplicitly says it is independent from. Left unchanged in this commit since\nit is not a security vulnerability and changing ~10 test files was judged\nout of this task's scope; flagging it for an explicit decision rather than\nsilently renaming it.\n\nNo product code, deterministic rules, AI-hypothesis logic, or knowledge-pack\nbehavior was touched. Full suite: 379 passed, 2 skipped (unchanged from\nbefore this commit). Package builds cleanly (sdist + wheel).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <redacted@example.invalid>",
